  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NMU: Fishforce Phase II - Addressing Fisheries Crime Through Training, Research and Cooperation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The FishFORCE project aims for Southern African countries to collaborate in cross border knowledge- and intelligence-led fisheries law enforcement to reduce illegal fishing and fisheries crimes in the region. Governments and intergovernmental organisations strengthen their fisheries and ocean policy frameworks for compliance and law enforcement. Involving SADC region countries including Kenya, Mauritius, Mozambique, Namibia, Tanzania and South Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
